WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.140
- All right everybody.

00:00:01.140 --> 00:00:03.720
I always end this show with a
fun story from the internet.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:05.191
This is "What I'm Liking".

00:00:05.191 --> 00:00:06.933
(playful music)

00:00:06.933 --> 00:00:07.980
(cheers)

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:10.350
When it comes to the eating
habits of college kids,

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.560
You probably picture late
night pizza and Top Ramen.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.490
I doubt a home cooked meal
ever enters the picture.

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:20.070
But that is not the case
at Kansas State University.

00:00:20.070 --> 00:00:21.660
Y'all a group of students have opened

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:24.120
their own home cooked pasta business

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.440
for just five bucks.

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:27.090
You get a heaping to-go box

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.500
of delicious homemade pasta

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.320
served right out their kitchen
window, which is incredible.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.350
They even make dessert
'cause they're awesome.

00:00:34.350 --> 00:00:36.360
It has students lining
up around the block.

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.250
Let's get these pasta
entrepreneurs in here.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:39.083
Everybody say hello

00:00:39.083 --> 00:00:41.460
to Santino, Quinn, Kennedy and Tyler

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:44.572
watching on Kansas teen topica.

00:00:44.572 --> 00:00:46.526
What's up y'all?

00:00:46.526 --> 00:00:48.870
- Not too much We're
just excited to be here.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.900
- I am- I love this story so much.

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.330
So I mean, I feel like
usually college kids

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:55.680
are just grabbing stuff

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:57.660
and not actually cooking ever.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.060
So Santino and Quinn, where
did you even get this idea?

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:01.110
Where'd it come from?

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:04.863
- Yeah, so it goes way
back to my hometown in KC.

00:01:04.863 --> 00:01:08.490
I got a Sicilian family
and of course I'm going to

00:01:08.490 --> 00:01:11.430
know how to cook pasta one of these days.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:14.040
So we always had Pasta
Sundays back at home

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.160
and as soon as we moved
to college I decided,

00:01:17.160 --> 00:01:19.392
hey, I want to continue
the Pasta Sunday tradition.

00:01:19.392 --> 00:01:21.554
And I continued to make the sauce

00:01:21.554 --> 00:01:24.782
and serve my friends and they've loved it.

00:01:24.782 --> 00:01:26.390
- Yeah. Yes we have

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.010
- Yes. And it got to
the point where people

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.740
random people on campus
were just noticing us

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:33.030
and calling us the pasta boys.

00:01:33.030 --> 00:01:36.150
So that's when we decided
to expand our operation

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:36.983
a little bit.

00:01:36.983 --> 00:01:39.892
Now, a few Sundays every month
we have our Pasta Sundays

00:01:39.892 --> 00:01:42.720
serve hundreds of people every time.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.585
And we just kind of
serve until we run out.

00:01:44.585 --> 00:01:45.540
- Yeah.

00:01:45.540 --> 00:01:47.790
- It can get kind of chaotic,
but it's a lot of fun.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:48.623
- It's so fun, yeah.

00:01:48.623 --> 00:01:49.710
- It's incredibly cool.

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.743
So Kennedy and Tyler, who does what?

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.280
- So we really all just play
off of our own strengths.

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:58.950
So Tino's obviously the
mastermind behind the whole thing.

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.139
He cooks all the pasta.

00:02:00.139 --> 00:02:01.080
- The only Italian.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:04.110
- Yeah. And Tyler's the money guy.

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:05.340
He handles all the money.

00:02:05.340 --> 00:02:07.110
And then we've got Quinn over here

00:02:07.110 --> 00:02:09.030
who boxes and preps all the orders,

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:11.370
hands 'em out the window
with smiling face.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:14.190
And I'm the social media
and marketing manager.

00:02:14.190 --> 00:02:17.670
I'm a student at the School
of Medias and Communication

00:02:17.670 --> 00:02:18.750
here at K State.

00:02:18.750 --> 00:02:20.160
And I really know the power of like

00:02:20.160 --> 00:02:23.430
getting a message out onto
social media platforms.

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:24.750
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And I just knew

00:02:24.750 --> 00:02:27.840
that our community needed to
know what these guys were doing

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:29.940
and it's been crazy turning them

00:02:29.940 --> 00:02:32.470
into overnight internet
sensations from this.

00:02:32.470 --> 00:02:33.360
- Yes.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.070
- And nothing would've been possible.

00:02:35.070 --> 00:02:36.420
without the help of Kennedy.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.740
She makes us look a lot better

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:39.270
than we actually look, which is awesome.

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.103
- Yeah.

00:02:40.103 --> 00:02:42.090
- But it's just been a great
experience here at K State.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:42.923
The whole community

00:02:42.923 --> 00:02:45.330
whether it be students
coming to get a cheap meal

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:47.130
or just families walking down the street

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:48.600
they've all really embraced us.

00:02:48.600 --> 00:02:49.800
We definitely feel like we're excited.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.749
Maybe want to expand the
operations, maybe do a food truck.

00:02:52.749 --> 00:02:54.060
- Yeah.
- Something like that.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:55.440
But for the time being

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.080
we're having a really good time
just embracing the community

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.700
and making lots of of good pasta.

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:00.533
- Yeah

00:03:00.533 --> 00:03:01.366
- That is so-

00:03:01.366 --> 00:03:03.630
I love the the pasta,
like the food truck idea.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:05.910
But it is incredibly awesome and funny

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.386
that you just serve it
right out your window.

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:09.350
Like that's incredible. I love that.

00:03:09.350 --> 00:03:12.750
The Pasta Boys and Girl were
kind enough to send me a plate.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:13.590
So I'm trying it.

00:03:13.590 --> 00:03:14.610
Here we go.

00:03:14.610 --> 00:03:16.590
I love my job.

00:03:16.590 --> 00:03:17.940
I get paid to eat y'all.

00:03:17.940 --> 00:03:18.900
This is incredible.

00:03:18.900 --> 00:03:19.733
Hold on.

00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:20.566
This is hard to do.

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:21.989
And look, you know, classy.

00:03:21.989 --> 00:03:23.223
Whatever, screw it.

00:03:26.455 --> 00:03:28.280
(muffled) This is so good!

00:03:28.280 --> 00:03:31.280
(audience cheering)

00:03:33.090 --> 00:03:35.670
Santino, Quinn, Kennedy and Tyler

00:03:35.670 --> 00:03:38.550
I'm liking your post right
now while cleaning my teeth.

00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:39.690
Y'all, that's not all.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.324
Our season long partner
pilot pen makers of friction,

00:03:41.324 --> 00:03:43.680
the go-to erasable pen of
the Kelly Clarkson Show

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:46.680
want to celebrate student
entrepreneurs just like you.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.230
So they're putting a thousand
dollars in your tip jar.

00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:50.063
How's that sound?

00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:51.081
(audience cheering)

00:03:51.081 --> 00:03:54.081
(students cheering)

00:03:54.928 --> 00:03:57.054
- Thank you so much.
- Thank you, Kelly.

00:03:57.054 --> 00:03:59.589
Congratulations on being a success guys.

00:03:59.589 --> 00:04:00.600
Keep it up.

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.433
Thank you.

00:04:01.433 --> 00:04:02.700
And thank you to all our guests this hour.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:04.860
Craig Robinson, Moose Weekes

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:07.680
Zeus McClurkin, Quinta
Brunson, Shirley Ralph,

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.110
Lisa Ann Walter, Nancy Lorraine,

00:04:10.110 --> 00:04:12.450
Carolyn Clifford, Simon Shacket

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:16.230
and all our friends at W X
Y Z, Channel Seven Detroit.

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:17.154
Y'all have a great day and if it's not,

00:04:17.154 --> 00:04:18.513
try some pasta.

